          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A graded bimonoid is like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoid"} bimonoid
            but graded, as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+monoid"} graded monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_{n})_{n \ge 0}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
          %p Whereas we’re not sure if the notion of graded bimonoid under this form is new or not, the notion of special graded bimonoid below is certainly.
          %p
            Under the conjecture of the page
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+powers+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+%28Q+plus%29-linear+category"} symmetric powers in a symmetric monoidal (Q plus)-linear category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+powers"} symmetric powers
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{1}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A graded bimonoid in a
